    {
      "id": "dcd9e323986ec6cd6c93ddbee3b3c0abaf43b174",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1978030114,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Sorry, in hindsight, I could have clarified more.\n\nThe Wireshark build system supports providing additional CMake commands through a \"CMakeListsCustom.txt\" file. This is done by calling the `ADD_CUSTOM_CMAKE_INCLUDE` macro (defined in the changed file) in \"CMakeLists.txt\" with no arguments.\nHowever, the definition of the macro implies that if an argument is provided, it will be used as the name(s) of the file(s) to be included; otherwise, it defaults to \"CMakeListsCustom.txt\".\n\nI encountered this when I added another call to `ADD_CUSTOM_CMAKE_INCLUDE` in \"CMakeLists.txt\", but with arguments, yet CMake did not include the new files as expected. As-is, the bug is currently not triggered, unless a developer performs a call to the macro with arguments.",
          "author": {
            "id": 14486151,
            "username": "hazimeh",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Ahmad Hazimeh",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/94628d37403dd3bbc1f750797b03c35d984ff1e221de4aaafb7111a1415c4a19?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/hazimeh"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-07-02T07:25:31.527Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-07-02T07:25:31.527Z",
